  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is running hot and Hicksville is surging\u2014but Glen Cove demands immediate action.\n\n**Port Washington:** Yesterday's $4,188 looks flat on headline revenue, but it's actually strong execution. Grooming revenue jumped 9% despite one fewer groomer than last Thursday; your team produced $642 per groomer against a 30-day baseline of $481\u201433% above trend. The concern: retail cratered 42% ($488 vs $839), and add-on attach dropped from 54% to 50%. This isn't a calendar miss; it's operational. Upsell discipline and front-of-house focus have softened. Week-to-date you're up 6%, but October MTD sits at $85,523 vs. a DOW-adjusted expectation of $89,708\u2014a real 4.7% performance gap. Retail is bleeding. Restock X-Small Treat Table, Braided Bully 12\", and Bully Sticks immediately (all zero inventory, 15\u201330 unit monthly burn).\n\n**Hicksville:** This is your win. October is up 20% YTD with 23% more appointments than September, and DOW-adjusted you're *beating* expectation by 8.7%\u2014that's genuine demand and execution. Core groom revenue climbed 10%. But add-ons tanked 48% (from $115 to $60); same operational signal as Port Washington. You're hitting capacity with 2.9 groomer-days per day and trending 9% higher productivity than baseline. The structural gap is bather hours\u2014Hicksville runs zero; Port Washington averaged 7.8 yesterday. That's a capacity unlock if you staff it.\n\n**Glen Cove:** Yesterday's 51% revenue drop is catastrophic\u2014but look at capacity: only 2 groomers scheduled, producing $95 each against a $237 baseline. That's not a market problem; it's a scheduling failure. Today and tomorrow you have zero groomers on the books. This store is bleeding $318k in Port Washington's lapse pool plus $139k in Hicksville's; Glen Cove isn't yet tracked separately, but it's operating as a cash drain, not a location.\n\n**Port Washington today:** 6 groomers, 15.0h bathers; tomorrow 4 groomers, 8.0h bathers; next 7 days 36 groomer-days. **Hicksville today:** 5 groomers, 0.0h bathers; tomorrow 4 groomers, 0.0h bathers; next 7 days"
